*> The edit-server screen (US2-1; 08 §10.8.6 edit_server texts): the server name and address
*> fields (a click focuses one; typed text, any keyboard layout, goes into the focused one;
*> Backspace deletes its last character; Enter is Done), Done and Cancel.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. EDIT-SERVER-BUILD.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, GUI width, GUI height.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLCONST.
 01 WS-KIND                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ACTION              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-W                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-H                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 20.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ZERO2               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-STATE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(80).
 01 WS-KEY-LENGTH          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(512).
 01 WS-Z1                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-Z2                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-Z3                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-GW                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-GH                   BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-GW L-GH.
     MOVE WK-LABEL TO WS-KIND
     COMPUTE WS-X = L-GW / 2 - 100
     MOVE 20 TO WS-Y
     MOVE "cobolcraft.screen.edit_server.title_add" TO WS-KEY
     IF SM-EDIT-INDEX > 0
         MOVE "cobolcraft.screen.edit_server.title_edit" TO WS-KEY
     END-IF
     MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-KEY)) TO WS-KEY-LENGTH
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-Z1 WS-X WS-Y WS-Z2 WS-Z3 WS-KEY
         WS-KEY-LENGTH
     MOVE 48 TO WS-Y
     MOVE "cobolcraft.screen.edit_server.name" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 34 TO WS-KEY-LENGTH
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-Z1 WS-X WS-Y WS-Z2 WS-Z3 WS-KEY
         WS-KEY-LENGTH
     MOVE 98 TO WS-Y
     MOVE "cobolcraft.screen.edit_server.address" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 37 TO WS-KEY-LENGTH
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-Z1 WS-X WS-Y WS-Z2 WS-Z3 WS-KEY
         WS-KEY-LENGTH
     MOVE WK-FIELD TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 200 TO WS-W
     MOVE 58 TO WS-Y
     MOVE ACT-FIELD-NAME TO WS-ACTION
     MOVE 0 TO WS-STATE
     IF SM-FOCUS = 1
         MOVE 1 TO WS-STATE
     END-IF
     MOVE SM-EDIT-NAME TO WS-TEXT
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-ACTION WS-Z1 WS-X WS-Y WS-W WS-H WS-TEXT
         SM-EDIT-NAME-LENGTH WS-STATE
     MOVE 108 TO WS-Y
     MOVE ACT-FIELD-ADDRESS TO WS-ACTION
     MOVE 0 TO WS-STATE
     IF SM-FOCUS = 2
         MOVE 1 TO WS-STATE
     END-IF
     MOVE SM-EDIT-ADDR TO WS-TEXT
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-ACTION WS-Z1 WS-X WS-Y WS-W WS-H WS-TEXT
         SM-EDIT-ADDR-LENGTH WS-STATE
     MOVE WK-BUTTON TO WS-KIND
     MOVE 98 TO WS-W
     MOVE 144 TO WS-Y
     MOVE ACT-DONE TO WS-ACTION
     MOVE "cobolcraft.screen.common.done" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 29 TO WS-KEY-LENGTH
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-ACTION WS-X WS-Y WS-W WS-H WS-KEY
         WS-KEY-LENGTH
     ADD 102 TO WS-X
     MOVE ACT-CANCEL TO WS-ACTION
     MOVE "cobolcraft.screen.common.cancel" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 31 TO WS-KEY-LENGTH
     CALL "WIDGET-ADD-KEY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KIND WS-ACTION WS-X WS-Y WS-W WS-H WS-KEY
         WS-KEY-LENGTH
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM EDIT-SERVER-BUILD.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. EDIT-SERVER-INPUT.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE: typed code points (UTF-8 encoded) are appended to the focused field while it
*> has room; Backspace removes the field's last character; Enter does Done.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CCSHIM.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BYTES               PIC X(4).
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ACTION              BINARY-LONG VALUE 9.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-Z1                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-Z2                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-Z3                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE.
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > IN-TEXT-COUNT
         CALL "UTF8-ENCODE" USING IN-TEXT(WS-I) WS-BYTES WS-COUNT
         EVALUATE TRUE
             WHEN SM-FOCUS = 1 AND SM-EDIT-NAME-LENGTH + WS-COUNT <= 64
                 MOVE WS-BYTES(1:WS-COUNT) TO SM-EDIT-NAME(SM-EDIT-NAME-LENGTH + 1:WS-COUNT)
                 ADD WS-COUNT TO SM-EDIT-NAME-LENGTH
             WHEN SM-FOCUS = 2 AND SM-EDIT-ADDR-LENGTH + WS-COUNT <= 256
                 MOVE WS-BYTES(1:WS-COUNT) TO SM-EDIT-ADDR(SM-EDIT-ADDR-LENGTH + 1:WS-COUNT)
                 ADD WS-COUNT TO SM-EDIT-ADDR-LENGTH
         END-EVALUATE
     END-PERFORM
     IF IN-KEY-PRESSED(CC-KEY-BACKSPACE + 1) = 1
         EVALUATE SM-FOCUS
             WHEN 1
                 CALL "TEXT-DROP-LAST" USING SM-EDIT-NAME SM-EDIT-NAME-LENGTH
             WHEN 2
                 CALL "TEXT-DROP-LAST" USING SM-EDIT-ADDR SM-EDIT-ADDR-LENGTH
         END-EVALUATE
     END-IF
     IF IN-KEY-PRESSED(CC-KEY-ENTER + 1) = 1
         CALL "SCREEN-ACTION" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ACTION WS-ZERO
     END-IF
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM EDIT-SERVER-INPUT.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEXT-DROP-LAST.
*> USING text area, length: removes the last UTF-8 character (its continuation bytes too).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-B                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 B-TEXT                 PIC X(1024) BASED.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-TEXT                 PIC X.
 01 L-LENGTH               BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-TEXT L-LENGTH.
     SET ADDRESS OF B-TEXT TO ADDRESS OF L-TEXT
     MOVE 128 TO WS-B
     PERFORM UNTIL L-LENGTH = 0 OR WS-B < 128 OR WS-B >= 192
         COMPUTE WS-B = FUNCTION ORD(B-TEXT(L-LENGTH:1)) - 1
         MOVE SPACE TO B-TEXT(L-LENGTH:1)
         SUBTRACT 1 FROM L-LENGTH
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TEXT-DROP-LAST.
